.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Lorenz&#x27;s 1963 convection model \dot x = \sigma(y - x), \dot y = x(\rho - z) - y, \dot z = xy - \beta z is fully deterministic, yet for \sigma = 10, \rho = 28, \beta = 8/3 its orbits wind forever around a butterfly-shaped strange attractor. This script repeats Lorenz&#x27;s accidental experiment: restart a run from a state rounded to three decimal places, and watch the two forecasts agree for a while, then diverge completely.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/ode_dynamics/chaotic_flows/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_lorenz_butterfly_effect_thumb.png
